Translations
------------
As an exception to the list above, you may, without asking first, copy and edit
the language files in Plateau/Locales and the template in localization for the
sole purpose of preparing a translation of Plateau Nameplates and sending it to
the copyright holder, for example as a pull request or issue on the official
GitHub repository.

By sending a translation, you confirm that you wrote it or personally checked
every line of it, that you have the right to send it, and you grant the
copyright holder a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable license to
use, modify and distribute it as part of Plateau Nameplates. Translators who
want to be credited will be named in the README and changelog.

This exception does not allow you to distribute Plateau Nameplates, a translated
copy of it, or its language files yourself.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.
IN NO EVENT SHALL THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE USE OF THE SOFTWARE.

